# Covers: a watcher body that cancels a LATER watcher must not truncate
#         the rest of the drain.
#
# Five watchers observe Realm.go / Realm.wpend in registration order:
#   P (at)        — appends "P"
#   W (whenever)  — appends "W" and clears its own condition
#   A (at sync)   — the cascade trigger: its inline body calls t2.stop()
#   B (at, t2-owned) — cancelled by A before the drain reaches it
#   C (at)        — must still fire after the cancellation
#
# Expected: Realm.hits == "PWC".  B never fires (its tag was stopped
# earlier in the same drain); P, W and C each fire exactly once.
#
# WHY IT CANNOT REGRESS THE OLD WAY.  The old core unlinked a cancelled
# watcher from the active list immediately, so the pre-captured successor
# of the watcher being processed could have a NULL next pointer and the
# pass silently stopped there — which needed a rescan, which needed a
# per-pass stamp to keep a level-triggered whenever from firing twice on
# the re-visit.  None of that exists now: cancelling only clears `armed`,
# and the list is compacted by a sweep that runs outside the walk, so the
# walk's `next` pointer stays valid and every watcher is visited once.
#
# W is a `whenever`, which is a reactive LOOP: it re-fires on body
# completion while its condition still holds, so its body clears the
# latch it watches.  Both writes on the trigger line are joined by `|`
# (atomic, no yield) so a single drain sees both.
#
## timeout: 30
## host: run Realm.hits = ""
## host: run Realm.go = false
## host: run Realm.wpend = false
## host: run var t2 = Tag.new()
## host: run at (Realm.go) { Realm.hits = Realm.hits + "P" }
## host: run whenever (Realm.wpend) { Realm.hits = Realm.hits + "W"; Realm.wpend = false }
## host: run at sync (Realm.go) { t2.stop() }
## host: run t2: at (Realm.go) { Realm.hits = Realm.hits + "B" }
## host: run at (Realm.go) { Realm.hits = Realm.hits + "C" }
## host: run Realm.wpend = true | Realm.go = true
## host: step 100000
## host: run Realm.hits
[00000000] ""
[00000000] false
[00000000] false
[00000000] <Tag>
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] true
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] "PWC"
